# Declares Service as a QML singleton: ONE instance for the whole shell engine,
# not one per importing component.
#
# The bar builds a widget per bar surface, and a bar surface exists per
# monitor. Everything instantiated inside the widget therefore existed once per
# monitor -- including `tonearmctl subscribe`, so a two-monitor setup held two
# persistent subscriptions to tonearmd and a three-monitor setup held three.
#
# NOT the same thing as `.pragma library`, which is its opposite: a .js file
# without that pragma gets one instance PER importing component, which is why
# Model.js passes shared tables per call instead of holding them. A QML
# singleton gets one instance for the engine. Do not "fix" this file by
# reasoning from that one.
singleton Service 1.0 Service.qml
